  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Polypodium vulgare",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polypodium_vulgare",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1369859374,
      "text": "Polypodium vulgare, the common polypody, is an evergreen fern of the family Polypodiaceae. The name is derived from Greek poly- (\"many\") and pous, podos (\"foot\"). Polypody has traditional uses in cooking for its aroma and sweet taste, and in herbal medicine as a purgative and vermifuge. This species is expansive and highly adapted to many environments."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Polypodium vulgare",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polypodium_vulgare",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 171581251,
      "text": "El polipodio común es una especie de helechos de la familia Polypodiaceae."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Polypode commun",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polypode_commun",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 232098550,
      "text": "Le Polypode commun est une espèce de fougère de la famille des Polypodiaceae. Il est parfois appelé réglisse des bois ou réglisse sauvage. En effet, son rhizome a été utilisé à des fins médicinales, mais aussi gastronomiques."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Polypodium vulgare",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polypodium_vulgare",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29661276,
      "text": "Polypodium vulgare, adalah sebuah spesies tumbuhan paku malar hijau pada famili Polypodiaceae. Namanya berasla dari bahasa Yunani poly- (\"banyak\") dan pous, podos (\"kaki\"). Tumbuhan ini memiliki kegunaan tradisional dalam memasak karena wangi dan rasanya yang manis, serta pada pengobatan tradisional sebagai pencahar dan obat cacing."
    }
  },
